    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0258" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24400: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-31T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>196 Your July 28th, 2 P.M. Seek early interview with Covarrubias<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d181-f1"/> and inform him that this Government confidently expects
                    that instructions will be given Commanders, Expeditionary Forces, <pb
                        facs="0259" n="159" xml:id="pg159"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> Lower California, to avoid provoking
                    hostilities near international frontier, whereby American lives and property may
                    be imperiled.</p>
                <p>Point out danger to entire Imperial Valley, California, of any accidental or
                    intentional interruption irrigation canals, upon which the very existence of
                    60,000 Americans depend[s].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d181-f1" n="19" xml:id="d181-f1-content">
                <p>Miguel Covarrubias, Secretary of Foreign Affairs of the Huerta Government.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
